Canada (Wagner 1972). This isolated Canadian occurrence is presumably the result of long-distance dispersal. Wagner (1972) noted that the British Columbia population of this 'south-temperate to subtropical fern is flourishing in the runnels of a system of hot springs, an obviously unusual site.' Jim Peck (pers. comm.) pointed out that 'likewise, it occurs on tufa of hot springs in Hot Springs, AR.'" />
