the species in wc AR in May). However, when fertile, the vertically oriented sporangia-bearing part sticks well above the prostrate blade portion that is often interwoven in the turf. Thus, as pointed out by Nelson (2000), the 'most effective way to find this fern is to search for it in closely cut lawns, especially cemeteries, by crawling on hands and knees or by laying one’s face close to the ground, then looking laterally across the top of the grass for the fertile frond segments.'" />
