 occurrence is presumably the result of long-distance dispersal. Also see page 37 for a possible explanation of the disjunct distribution of this species from TX to s Mexico. Ophioglossum vulgatum can be confused with O. petiolatum but, in addition to the characters in the key, it has unusually persistent leathery basal leaf sheaths (these ephemeral in O. petiolatum) (Thomas 1979; Wagner &amp; Wagner 1993)." />
