ished as var. erythrolepis and the c and s Mexico populations are clearly var. polylepis, there are intervening areas where 'a broad range of intergradation between the varieties occurs' (Wendt 1980). Because of its rareness and limited distribution in the state, we consider this species to be of conservation concern in TX." />
